    <!-- PREAMBLE -->
    <section class="preamble">
      <div class="preamble-label">Preamble</div>
      <div class="preamble-body">
        <p>The SEO industry sells reports on rankings that no longer decide the purchase. AI assistants decide who gets named now, and most sites are invisible to them. The tools sold to fix it read one number and call it a strategy. That is guessing at scale.</p>
        <p>We are the measurement layer that industry never built. We correlate three sources, refuse single-source recommendations, publish deltas per signal, and hand you the spec. Your team ships, or ours does. Either way, every claim carries the receipt that earned it.</p>
        <p>This is the document that explains why. <em>Read it once. Bookmark it. Come back when you need the reminder.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE MANIFESTO BODY -->
    <section class="doc-body">
      <div class="doc-body-label">The Manifesto · Read as one paragraph.</div>
      <div class="doc-body-copy">
        <p>This is the new reality. AI decides who gets found now. It reads every site before it names one. Most sites are invisible. Their owners never know. Their agencies ship and move on. A dashboard, a promise, no proof. That's not how you win. <span class="real">Real decisions</span> come from <span class="real">real data</span>, and real data is the one thing nobody handed you. Most site structure is flawed and no one has called it out. Schema shells with no keys. Dead canonicals. Reviews rotting in iframes no crawler will read. AI bots blocked from reading the site. We put the truth on the table. And here's what they missed: the same broken code hiding you from AI is burying you in Google too. Fix it once, win both. <span class="real">Real</span> data correlated directly to your business goals. We're not another agency selling fake certainty. We build with our hands. We measure what's real. We prove it or we say nothing. Because <span class="real">real work</span> produces <span class="real">real outcomes</span>. Cited by the machines, ranked by search, earned, not guessed. The game isn't rigged beyond winning. Hard work still wins. Real still beats fake. We're fixing the code rotting the internet and raising the bar for every site that ships after ours. This is the line. We're drawing it. The revolution starts now.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PRINCIPLES -->
    <section class="principles">
      <div class="principles-label">Principles we hold</div>
      <h2 class="principles-h">The lines we <span class="ox">will not cross.</span></h2>
      <ol class="principles-list">
        <li>
          <div class="principle-num">01</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="principle-h">Three sources or nothing.</h3>
            <p class="principle-body">A finding only becomes a recommendation when at least two of three sources agree. AI answers, search performance, and site structure. Everything else is a note in the report, never the spec. We refuse to guess and we refuse to sell guessing dressed as certainty.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="principle-num">02</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="principle-h">Publish the receipt.</h3>
            <p class="principle-body">Every scan carries the version it was run under. Every recommendation carries the signals that surfaced it. Every re-scan publishes deltas per signal, per surface, per engine. If the numbers did not move, we tell you. If a category is structurally unwinnable, we tell you where the ceiling is.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="principle-num">03</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="principle-h">Neutral to the build.</h3>
            <p class="principle-body">We are the measurement layer that sits above whatever vendor stack you already have. We do not need to be your builder to be your measurement discipline. We get you the data. We don't care who makes the changes, as long as they get made correctly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="principle-num">04</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="principle-h">AI and search move together.</h3>
            <p class="principle-body">Both surfaces reward the same underlying structural legibility. Fix your site once, correctly, and AI citation climbs alongside search ranking. You are not betting on a speculative AI-only future. You are making structural fixes that pay off everywhere a customer looks for you.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="principle-num">05</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="principle-h">No advertising accepted.</h3>
            <p class="principle-body">The AI Visibility Index publishes quarterly. Named winners, named losers, original data across the top U.S. metros. Nobody pays to be in it or to move up in it. The measurement is not a marketing surface. The measurement is the credential.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
